hello and welcome to my very first uh  video update i hope you enjoy hearing  about all of the initiatives and  projects that we're working on across  northeast derbyshire over the coming  weeks and months  like many of you i've been deeply moved  by the distressing images that we've  seen coming out of afghanistan you may  have heard that the prime minister's  recently announced the operation warm  welcome is now underway and that's to  welcome afghan rivals into the uk  particularly those who supported the  uk during the conflict as well as their  families and evacuees who are at highest  risk  of reprisals and we're working to ensure  that they're supported as they rebuild  their lives over in the uk we've also  been pressing ahead with many new  projects to improve the lives of both  residents and visitors to our beautiful  part of derbyshire  we're investing a massive 1.9 million  pounds in kilometer sports centre and  creating even more facilities for  residents and visitors to enjoy  the works are going to start later on  this month and the improvements include  a large 80 station gym  fitness studios  a cafe  the creation of a large multi-story soft  play area  providing additional changing places  toilets and making the centre accessible  for non-sporting customers and a great  asset for the whole community for  everyday general use or to host  children's parties now keeping on the  subject of legislators we've also  received a humbling and heartfelt thanks  from the staff at the nhs who've been  working closely with our teams  at charlie park leisure centre which as  you will know has been a vaccination  centre for the last eight months  the vaccination operation has now moved  out of the centre and after incredibly  supporting 60 000 people in this  district to be vaccinated and saving  thousands of lives in the process  kate chilton the general manager of the  nhs operation who's been running the  vaccination program said i would like to  take this opportunity to thank you for  having us on site and nedc for providing  the facilities over the past eight  months  thank you to the whole team who have  been proactively supporting the campaign  and worked closely with the vaccination  team to make our stay with you run like  clockwork we absolutely couldn't have  achieved the mammoth 60 000 vaccinations  without your support  we're also investing 1.5 million pounds  in eckington swimming pool and fitness  centre  which will slash its carbon emissions by  66 percent and make it one of the  greenest leisure centres in the area the  project supports our efforts to  decarbonize energy sources in public  buildings to achieve net zero by 2030.  this includes the use of solar power  technology replacing gas-powered boilers  with air source heat pumps and a new air  handling system that will improve air  quality and will increase temperatures  in the pool for customers in the  building on the subject of technology  i'm delighted that we're now able to  help people develop their digital skills  through the new digital inclusion  project digital connect  free digital training is being offered  to residents who live in north east  derbyshire age 50 and above  more information about this can be found  on our website  as well as looking after our residents  our businesses are a key focus for us as  we move through the pandemic and beyond  from now until the end of november we're  encouraging businesses to share their  views to identify the skills they need  to help them thrive and grow  the business skills audit can be  completed now via our website so please  make sure that you have your say  our website and social media channels  also have updates about all the latest  fundraising that our chairman councillor  thaka is doing for ashgate hospice care  as well as some brilliant news about a  national accolade that the street scene  team have been awarded  so please do have a look and remember to  sign up to receive all the latest  updates from us so that you don't miss  out on our news and views and offers  from north east derbyshire district  council  when so many events have had to be  cancelled because of cobit i'm delighted  we're now able to commemorate our  commitment to the armed forces covenant  and pay tribute to our armed forces  community  please join us for this very special  armed forces celebration event which  will be held from 11 a.m to 3 p.m on  sunday the 3rd of october at drumfield  sports centre adjoining far water lane  car park more information will be on our  website and social media so please do  keep checking for the details  finally if you'd like to find out even  more about the work of the council and  our housing partner come along to one of  our meet the council events which will  be taking place on the 27th of september  at eckington civic center and on the 5th  of october at charlie park leisure  centre in clay cross both events run  from 5 30 to 7 30 p.m and will give  visitors the chance to speak with  officers and counsellors and raise  queries about services and find out  about our online services get advice and  guidance and quiz myself  fellow cabinet members and senior  officers on any issues that are  affecting your community finally before  i go i just would also like to welcome  councillors stratford stevenson and  councillor lacey who were successful  following the recent by-elections  and welcome to them to the council and  look forward to working with them thanks  very much for watching our video update  i hope you found it really useful but  please do give us any feedback on any  other issues you might like us to cover  and hopefully you'll you'll see from us  very very soon  you
 

